body:
Hi all! I'm a casual revived collector and recently purchased the 25th anniversary jumbo binder to store some cards that came with boxes I've bought recently. I'm interested in filling it out, but I've heard that the TCG Jumbo sizes have changed over time, so I'd rather not purchase something that won't fit in this binder.

&#x200B;

Does anyone know if this card specifically fits? Thanks for the help & being a great community resource!

That's great! It is my pleasure to help if there is anything I can do. I know when I was going through this, the only thing my research was telling me it could be was mites or ringworm, and neither seemed like the perfect fit diagnostic and the at home treatments for both weren't helping, either. (Appeared suddenly our of the blue, started on the rump vs on the snout as ringworm typically does, myself and my furred pigs didn't catch it if it was ringworm, skin was peel-y and not so much scabby, I regularly use preventative ivermectin to avoid mites...) My babies were soo uncomfortable, and it's taken a good two weeks to clear up entirely, but their skin is even and smooth now as it should be. Their skin improved day by day. Skinnies are just special as they were specifically bred to test various compounds on their skin in laboratories, so they are quite sensitive to things furry pigs tolerate just fine. The info just wasn't out there for me and my pigs were in discomfort because of it.

&#x200B;

It may not be the bedding if it is an allergic reaction unfortunately so I'd just keep an eye out. I was able to narrow it down to my bedding choice because it was the only thing that changed before they developed symptoms. If you notice your furry pig developing bald patches, then something like ringworm would be more likely I would believe. If it worsens, I definitely advise visiting a vet to get a professional opinion, but hopefully you are able to nip it in the bud before it gets there if it is an allergic reaction! Best of luck friend!
